g:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,860px)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-0","children":[["$","aside",null,{"className":"hidden lg:col-start-1 lg:block lg:justify-self-end lg:pr-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white sticky top-28 w-52 rounded-2xl p-6","children":["$","$L13",null,{"sections":[{"_key":"what-figma-weave-does-well","title":"What Weave does well"},{"_key":"where-teams-hit-friction","title":"The friction"},{"_key":"how-melius-approaches-the-same-work","title":"The Melius approach"},{"_key":"who-should-switch","title":"Who should switch"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"className":"w-full flex-col gap-4 overflow-visible md:static","linkClassName":"t-b-3 !font-semibold text-foreground-muted leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-gray-dark-1","activeLinkClassName":"text-orange"}]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"wysiwyg bg-white w-full min-w-0 rounded-3xl p-6 md:p-10 lg:col-start-2 lg:p-12","children":[["$","p","b1179",{"children":["Figma Weave, the product that started as Weavy before Figma acquired it, is a strong idea: a node-based generation canvas with real editing tools, compositing, masking, color grading, and a Timeline for sequencing, plus a set of one-click workflows surfaced right inside Figma Design. For designers who already live in Figma, having generation that close to their work is compelling."]}],["$","p","b1183",{"children":["That tight coupling is also the reason people search for a ",["$","strong","b1181",{"children":["Figma Weave alternative"]}],". If you don't live in Figma, or you want a standalone workspace with an agent and more predictable costs, the ecosystem fit becomes a constraint rather than a feature. Here's how Melius compares."]}],["$","h2","b1185",{"id":"what-figma-weave-does-well","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What Figma Weave does well"]}],["$","p","b1187",{"children":["Weave combines generation with genuine editing, compositing, masking and grading, not just prompt-in, image-out, and its node graph makes each step visible and re-runnable. The June 2026 Timeline brought video sequencing and sound onto the same canvas, and the embedded workflows make common design tasks a click away for anyone already in Figma. As a design-adjacent generation layer, it's well built."]}],"$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e"]}]]}]]}],"$L1f"]
