1e:["$","div","b1306",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best Figma Weave alternative?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Melius is the strongest standalone alternative to Figma Weave. Both are node-based generation canvases with broad model access, but Melius is an independent creative workspace rather than a layer tied to the Figma ecosystem, it adds Mel to plan and wire multi-step work, and it keeps every model under one credit pool."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How is Melius different from Figma Weave?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The biggest difference is the agent. Figma Weave has no AI agent, so its node graphs are wired and run by hand, and it is deeply tied to Figma's ecosystem. Melius is a standalone, agent-first workspace: Mel builds and runs the graph from a brief and also works in Slack, its MCP is canvas-level so an external agent like Claude can drive the canvas from any host, and every model shares one subscription."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Is Figma Weave the same as Weavy?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. Weavy was the original node-based generation canvas; Figma acquired it and rebranded it Figma Weave, folding it into Figma Design. So a Weavy alternative and a Figma Weave alternative are the same search. If you want that node-canvas-plus-generation model but without the Figma coupling, Melius is a standalone equivalent with an agent and one shared credit pool."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Why do people look for a Figma Weave alternative?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":"$L2f"}]]}],"$L30"]}],"$L31","$L32"]}]
1f:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L33","post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp",{"post":{"_key":"post-connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","slug":"connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp","category":"modus-news","title":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas with MCP","isoDate":"2026-07-20","date":"July 20, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Connect Claude to a creative canvas over MCP and skip the context drift you get from copy-pasting into a chatbot. The Model Context Protocol exposes the Melius canvas as live, structured data an agent can read and act on. Here is how to connect Claude to Melius, what the tools actually are, and why the loop self-corrects.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/connect-ai-agents-canvas-mcp/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the Model Context Protocol (MCP)?","answer":"MCP is an open standard that lets an AI agent connect to a server and call the tools and resources that server exposes. It started with IDEs and terminals, and the same pattern lets an agent read and act on a live creative canvas instead of a screenshot."},{"question":"What is Claude MCP?","answer":"Claude MCP just means using the Model Context Protocol with Claude as the host: Claude connects to an MCP server and calls the tools it exposes. Point it at the Melius connector and Claude can read and act on your live canvas directly, rather than working from a pasted description. The protocol is host-agnostic, so any MCP-compatible model works the same way."},{"question":"How do I connect Claude to Melius?","answer":"The recommended path is the hosted connector. Add a custom MCP connector in your host and point it at https://mcp.melius.com/mcp, then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. Melius mints a durable, revocable connector key for that team, so there is nothing to paste and nothing to refresh."},{"question":"Does the agent generate the images and video itself?","answer":"No. The host model (for example Claude) is the agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do. The images, video, and audio are produced by the generation models available on the platform, selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate."},{"question":"Can I use a model other than Claude?","answer":"Yes. Because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any MCP-compatible host. Melius is model-agnostic at the host level."},{"question":"What stops the agent from acting on nodes that no longer exist?","answer":"The platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas, so if it references something that is no longer there, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work","title":"The MCP bridge"},{"_key":"connecting-claude-to-melius","title":"Connecting Claude"},{"_key":"a-self-correcting-loop","title":"Self-correcting loop"},{"_key":"bring-your-own-model","title":"Bring your own model"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b717","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b714","text":"When you work with a large language model in a creative environment, the most common point of failure isn't the model's reasoning, it's the data it can see. Many workflows still rely on a copy-paste style, where a person describes a canvas, a prompt, or a generated result to a chatbot by hand. That inevitably leads to ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b715","text":"context drift","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b716","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b721","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b718","text":"Context drift is when an agent's understanding of a project diverges from the actual state of the work over time. Standard LLM chats are stateless and disconnected from the tool's live state, so the agent loses track of which nodes exist, how they're wired, and which generation produced which output. It might ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b719","text":"remember","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b720","text":" a video node from three prompts ago with no way of knowing it was since deleted, re-run with a different model, or rewired to a new source image. Without a protocol-level bridge, the model stays blind and you become the manual data translator.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b723","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b722","text":"A standard bridge for creative work","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-standard-bridge-for-creative-work"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b732","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b725","href":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b724","text":"Can a standard protocol close the gap between creative software and external AI models? The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b726","text":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)","marks":["b725"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b727","text":" helps by defining an open interface that lets an agent connect to a server and call its exposed ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b728","text":"tools","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b729","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b730","text":"resources","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b731","text":". The developer community first adopted MCP to connect LLMs to IDEs and terminals, but the same pattern applies to creative software: expose the workspace as structured, queryable data instead of a flat screenshot.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b740","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b733","text":"Melius does exactly this. Its canvas is organized as Team â†’ Projects â†’ Canvas â†’ Nodes + Edges â†’ Runs. A canvas is a 2D workspace; ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b734","text":"nodes","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b735","text":" are creative units (text prompts, images, videos, audio, files); ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b736","text":"edges","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b737","text":" wire nodes together to pass data between them; and a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b738","text":"run","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b739","text":" executes AI generation on a node, taking its prompt, model config, and upstream inputs and producing an output. Over MCP, an agent reads that live node-and-edge graph and acts on it directly, rather than guessing from a description.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b742","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b741","text":"Connecting Claude to Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"connecting-claude-to-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b749","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b746","href":"https://docs.melius.com/mcp/overview","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b743","text":"Connecting takes a couple of minutes. The quickest path is the hosted connector: add a custom MCP connector in your host, point it at ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b744","text":"https://mcp.melius.com/mcp","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b745","text":", then log in and pick a team when the authorize page opens. For the full walkthrough, including the local server for development and how credentials work, see the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b747","text":"Melius MCP docs","marks":["b746"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b748","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b751","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b750","text":"What the agent can actually do","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b753","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b752","text":"Once connected, the host gets a focused set of capabilities that mirror how the canvas works, rather than one opaque API. At a high level, an agent can:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b756","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b754","text":"Read the live canvas","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b755","text":": what's on it, how the pieces are wired together, and each one's current output, all from the same live state your browser sees","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b757","text":"Understand what's possible","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b758","text":": which generation models are available and what each one needs, so it works from real capabilities instead of guessing","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b762","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b760","text":"Compose the work","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b761","text":": add, arrange, and wire together the pieces of a creative pipeline","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b765","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b763","text":"Run and follow through","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b764","text":": kick off generations and act on the results as they come back","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b772","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b769","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b766","text":"So a prompt like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b767","text":"generate a product shot, then animate it into a 5-second clip","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b768","text":" becomes a short pipeline the agent assembles and runs on the real canvas, not a visual approximation. It is the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b770","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b769"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b771","text":" driven from your own agent. The exact shape of that surface is where a lot of the craft lives, so we'll leave the finer mechanics to the platform.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b774","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b773","text":"A self-correcting loop","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"a-self-correcting-loop"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b776","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b775","text":"One genuinely useful property falls out of exposing the canvas as structured data: the platform rejects stale or hallucinated references. Everything the agent points at has to resolve against the live canvas. If it references something that no longer exists, the call fails with a correction that sends it back to re-read the current state. A common failure mode, an agent confidently referencing something that isn't there, becomes a caught error and a re-scan, so the agent corrects itself instead of silently producing broken or failed work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b778","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b777","text":"Bring your own model","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"bring-your-own-model"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b782","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b779","text":"Melius is model-agnostic at the host level: because the connector speaks standard MCP, you can drive it from any compatible host. Keep the two ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b780","text":"models","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b781","text":" in play distinct. The host model is the reasoning agent that reads the canvas and decides what to do; the generation models, the ones that actually produce images, video, and audio, are the ones available on the platform and selected per node. The agent orchestrates; the media models generate.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b787","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b784","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b783","text":"By connecting the Melius MCP server, you aren't bolting on a black-box AI button, you're giving an external agent live, structured access to your canvas, so it has the context it needs to be genuinely useful. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b785","text":"Start creating with Melius","marks":["b784"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b786","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b789","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b788","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b790","items":"$1f:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"}]}}],"$L34","$L35"]}]]}]]}]
