30:["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"The dominant complaint is credit cost: users report credits burning extremely fast, sometimes thousands of credits for a few minutes of work, with iterative fixes for AI mistakes eating more. There are also reports of billing friction on cancellation, and some tooling is still in open beta. Teams outside the Figma ecosystem also want a standalone option."}]
31:["$","details","4",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Does Melius integrate with design tools?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Melius exposes an MCP server, so an agent like Claude can read and act on your canvas from your own environment. Rather than binding generation to one design suite, it aims to be model-agnostic and host-agnostic so it fits whatever workflow you already use."}]]}]
32:["$","details","5",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can Melius sequence video like Weave's Timeline?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes. Melius includes an in-app multi-track editor for arranging shots, timing and layering audio, alongside the node canvas for building the generations that feed it."}]]}]
34:["$","$L33","post-one-subscription-every-model",{"post":{"_key":"post-one-subscription-every-model","slug":"one-subscription-every-model","category":"modus-news","title":"One subscription, every model: an all-in-one AI aggregator guide","isoDate":"2026-07-17","date":"July 17, 2026","readTime":"7 Min Read","excerpt":"An AI aggregator puts every model, text, image, video and audio, under one subscription instead of a fragmented stack that clears $100 a month. Here is why aggregators are winning, what a true all-in-one creative AI platform must deliver, and a three-step plan to consolidate your workflow onto a single canvas.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/one-subscription-every-model/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?","answer":"Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs; it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, so you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack."},{"question":"What is subscription bloat, or the AI tax?","answer":"Subscription bloat is what happens when a creative stack is assembled one $20 tool at a time. Text generation, voiceover, image generation, and video generation each arrive as a separate subscription, and a typical stack easily clears $100 a month. The hidden cost isn't only the dollar amount, it's the friction of four interfaces, four credit systems, and four usage caps that can't share quota."},{"question":"What is an AI aggregator?","answer":"An AI aggregator is a platform that consolidates specialized generative engines, for image, video, and audio, into a single workflow and one billing umbrella. Instead of subscribing to each provider directly, you access frontier models like Kling and Seedance for video, GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana Pro for images, and ElevenLabs and Seed Audio for audio through one interface, with one credit pool and one place your assets live. The best aggregators go further, adding a shared context and an agent that orchestrates those models for you rather than just listing them."},{"question":"What is the best AI aggregator?","answer":"The best AI aggregator is the one that does more than list models behind one login. Look for three things: real API parity with the flagship models (so quality isn't sacrificed for convenience), one shared credit pool so you aren't rationing across silos, and an orchestration layer, a canvas plus an agent, that wires the models together and prompts each one correctly. Melius is built around exactly that: every major model on a node-based canvas, one credit pool, and Mel, an agent that plans and routes the work."},{"question":"Why does an aggregator get better results than using the models directly?","answer":"Because access to the models is only half the problem, the other half is orchestration. Melius is built on a node-based creative canvas where every prompt, image, video, and audio track is a connected node, so the output of one model can flow into the next and every generation shares the same brief and brand context. On top of that sits Mel, an agent that can see the whole graph, choose the right model for each step, wire the workflow together, and write the specific prompt each model responds to. A flat list of APIs can't do that, which is why context across models and agentic orchestration are what actually make the results land."},{"question":"What is model agnosticism, and why does it matter?","answer":"Model agnosticism means your workflow isn't locked to a single provider. When a new version of a model drops, an aggregator can add it to the existing dashboard, so you select it from a dropdown instead of buying another subscription or rebuilding your process. It lets you take a best-of-breed approach, testing one model for lighting and another for character consistency, for the price of one."},{"question":"How much can I save by consolidating AI subscriptions?","answer":"A fragmented stack of scripting, voiceover, imagery, and animation tools typically runs $82 to $102 per month. Moving that work onto a single aggregator can lower monthly costs by up to 60%, and it recovers the time otherwise lost to managing billing cycles and switching tabs."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"the-hidden-cost-of-the-fragmented-ai-stack","title":"The hidden cost"},{"_key":"defining-the-all-in-one-creative-standard","title":"The standard"},{"_key":"melius-consolidating-your-creative-workflow","title":"Consolidating"},{"_key":"why-the-canvas-and-the-agent-are-the-real-unlock","title":"Canvas & agent"},{"_key":"performance-vs-price-why-aggregators-are-winning","title":"Why aggregators win"},{"_key":"how-to-migrate-your-creative-projects-to-a-unified-platform","title":"How to migrate"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b527","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b526","text":"The math for a modern creative professional is increasingly broken. If you want the best text generation, you pay OpenAI $20. For high-end voiceovers, ElevenLabs takes another $22. If you need cinematic video generation, a Kling or Luma subscription adds roughly $30. Throw in a specialized image generator like Midjourney or a Flux-based tool for another $10 to $30, and your monthly AI tax easily clears $100.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b531","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b528","text":"This is ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b529","text":"subscription bloat","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b530","text":". We are living through the fragmented creative stack era, where creators spend as much time managing billing cycles and switching tabs as they do actually creating. The solution isn't to stop using these models, it's to change how you access them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b533","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b532","text":"The hidden cost of the fragmented AI stack","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-hidden-cost-of-the-fragmented-ai-stack"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b535","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b534","text":"The financial burden of AI is often underestimated because it creeps in $20 at a time. But the true cost isn't just the dollar amount, it's the friction. Consider a typical video production workflow:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b536","rows":[{"_key":"b537","cells":[{"_key":"b538","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b540","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b539","text":"Stage","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b541","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b543","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b542","text":"Typical tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b544","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b546","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b545","text":"Monthly cost","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b547","cells":[{"_key":"b548","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b550","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b549","text":"Scripting","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b551","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b553","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b552","text":"ChatGPT","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b554","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b556","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b555","text":"$$20","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b557","cells":[{"_key":"b558","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b560","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b559","text":"Voiceover","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b561","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b563","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b562","text":"ElevenLabs (Creator tier)","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b564","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b566","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b565","text":"$$22","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b567","cells":[{"_key":"b568","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b570","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b569","text":"Visuals","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b571","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b573","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b572","text":"Midjourney or Flux","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b574","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b576","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b575","text":"$$10â€“$30","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b577","cells":[{"_key":"b578","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b580","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b579","text":"Animation","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b581","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b583","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b582","text":"Kling AI or Luma Dream Machine","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b584","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b586","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b585","text":"$$30","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b587","cells":[{"_key":"b588","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b590","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b589","text":"Total","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b591","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b593","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b592","text":"Four interfaces, four silos","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b594","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b596","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b595","text":"$$82â€“$102","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b598","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b597","text":"This fragmented stack forces you to navigate four different interfaces, four different credit systems, and four different usage caps. If you hit a limit on Kling, you can't borrow credits from your unused ElevenLabs quota. You're locked into silos. This inefficiency is the primary driver behind the rise of AI aggregators, platforms that consolidate these specialized engines into a single, cohesive workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b600","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b599","text":"Defining the all-in-one creative standard","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"defining-the-all-in-one-creative-standard"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b604","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b601","text":"Not every platform that claims to be all-in-one actually delivers. Many are simply LLM wrappers, interfaces that connect to a chat model and maybe one basic image generator. To be a true creative powerhouse, a platform must master the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b602","text":"Triple Threat","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b603","text":" of modalities:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b607","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b605","text":"Image generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b606","text":"A spread of state-of-the-art models like GPT Image 2, Nano Banana Pro, and Seedream, which handle text-in-image, style control, and anatomical accuracy far better than older models. No single one wins every brief, so you want the choice.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b610","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b608","text":"Video generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b609","text":"Access to frontier models like Kling and Seedance, capable of consistent physics and high-resolution motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b613","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b611","text":"Audio generation. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b612","text":"High-fidelity voice synthesis and music from ElevenLabs, plus reference-driven voices from ByteDance's Seed Audio.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b615","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b614","text":"When evaluating a unified platform, use this checklist to make sure you aren't sacrificing quality for convenience:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b618","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b616","text":"API parity. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b617","text":"Does the platform offer the same settings (guidance scale, seed control, aspect ratios) as the native tools?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b621","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b619","text":"Model latency. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b620","text":"Is there a significant delay between clicking generate and the model responding?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b624","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b622","text":"Modal diversity. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b623","text":"Does it cover the full Triple Threat, or is it heavily weighted toward just text?","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b626","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b625","text":"Melius: consolidating your creative workflow","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"melius-consolidating-your-creative-workflow"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b640","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b627","text":"Melius is built specifically to bridge the gap between high-end generative power and cost-efficiency. By integrating frontier models like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b628","text":"Kling","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b629","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b630","text":"Seedance","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b631","text":" for video, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b632","text":"GPT Image 2","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b633","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b634","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b635","text":" for imagery, and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b636","text":"ElevenLabs","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b637","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b638","text":"Seed Audio","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b639","text":" for audio under one billing umbrella, it eliminates the need for a dozen separate logins.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b642","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b641","text":"Can a single subscription truly replace specialized AI tools without losing quality?","marks":["strong"]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b644","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b643","text":"Yes, provided the platform maintains direct API parity with flagship models like Kling and ElevenLabs. Melius achieves this by acting as a unified creative canvas where you can generate a cinematic shot in Kling, overlay a voiceover from ElevenLabs, and refine the prompt with a frontier text model, all within the same interface. This consolidation doesn't just lower monthly costs by up to 60%, it removes the cognitive load of switching contexts, letting you focus on the narrative rather than the tech stack.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b648","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b645","text":"The advantage here isn't just the unified billing, it's the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b646","text":"unified interface","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b647","text":". In a fragmented stack, your assets are scattered across four different gallery pages. In Melius, your video, audio, and images live in a single project ecosystem, making it significantly easier to iterate on a concept without losing your momentum.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b650","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b649","text":"Why the canvas and the agent are the real unlock","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-the-canvas-and-the-agent-are-the-real-unlock"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b656","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b651","text":"Access to every model is table stakes. A dropdown of frontier engines is only as good as your ability to point the right one at the right job and prompt it well, and that is exactly where a bare LLM wrapper falls down. Melius is built on two things a flat list of models doesn't have: a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b652","text":"node-based creative canvas","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b653","text":" and an ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b654","text":"agentic harness","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b655","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b666","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b660","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false},{"_type":"link","_key":"b663","href":"/blog/seedance-2-5-anticipation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b657","text":"On the canvas, every prompt, image, video clip, and audio track is a node, and the edges between them carry data from one step to the next. An image node feeds a video node, a script node feeds a voiceover, a still becomes the key frame for a shot. The structure of your project is visible and connected, not buried in a dozen separate chat histories. That shared graph is what gives the platform ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b658","text":"context across models","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b659","text":": the output of a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b661","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["b660"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b662","text":" image can flow directly into a Kling or ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b664","text":"Seedance","marks":["b663"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b665","text":" video, and the same brief and brand context inform every generation on the board.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b670","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b667","text":"Sitting on top of that canvas is Mel, the built-in creative-director agent. Because Mel can see the whole graph, it does the part most people get wrong on their own: it ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b668","text":"orchestrates","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b669","text":" the work. It decides which model fits each step, wires the nodes together in the right order, and translates your intent into the specific prompt each model actually responds to. Kling wants motion described a certain way; an image model wants composition and lens; ElevenLabs wants direction on tone and pacing. Mel handles that per-model prompt craft so you don't have to learn the quirks of ten different tools.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b677","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b674","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b671","text":"This is why the platform gets more ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b672","text":"right","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b673","text":" than a raw list of APIs ever could. The models are the engines, but the canvas gives them shared context and the agent knows how to drive them. A single creative director can hand Mel a brief and get back a coherent, multi-model workflow, generated, connected, and on-brand, the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b675","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b674"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b676","text":" in one place, instead of manually copying assets between four tabs and re-explaining the concept to each one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b679","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b678","text":"Performance vs. price: why aggregators are winning","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"performance-vs-price-why-aggregators-are-winning"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b681","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b680","text":"The legacy model of AI subscriptions asks you to bet on a single horse. If you subscribe to one specific video generator, you're stuck with their version of reality for the month. If a better model drops two weeks later, you're either stuck or paying for a second subscription.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b685","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b682","text":"The aggregator model offers ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b683","text":"model agnosticism","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b684","text":". This is the ultimate future-proofing for a creator. When a new version of Flux or a new competitor to Kling is released, an aggregator like Melius can integrate it into the existing dashboard. You don't have to change your workflow or update your billing, you just select the new model from a dropdown.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b687","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b686","text":"This flexibility allows for a best-of-breed approach. You might find that for a specific project, one model handles lighting better while another handles character consistency. On an aggregator platform, you can test both for the price of one, rather than being locked into the limitations of a single provider.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b689","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b688","text":"How to migrate your creative projects to a unified platform","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"how-to-migrate-your-creative-projects-to-a-unified-platform"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b691","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b690","text":"Transitioning from a fragmented stack to a unified platform like Melius doesn't have to happen overnight. Here is a practical three-step plan to reclaim your workflow.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b694","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b692","text":"The subscription audit. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b693","text":"List every AI tool you currently pay for. Identify the usage gap, models you pay $20 a month for but only use three or four times. These are the first candidates for consolidation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b697","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b695","text":"The output benchmark. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b696","text":"Before canceling your standalone subscriptions, run your most common prompts through Melius. Compare the Kling video output or the ElevenLabs voice clarity against the native apps. With proper API integration, you'll find the results are identical.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b700","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b698","text":"Centralize your assets. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b699","text":"Start a new project within Melius and generate all assets (image, video, and audio) for that specific campaign in the unified canvas. Once you experience the lack of tab-switching, the friction of the old fragmented way becomes much more apparent.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b705","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b702","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b701","text":"The era of paying for five different $20 subscriptions is ending. By moving to a unified platform, you aren't just saving money, you're buying back the time and mental energy required to actually be a creator. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b703","text":"Start creating with Melius","marks":["b702"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b704","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b707","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b706","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b708","items":"$34:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b713","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b710","href":"/blog/ai-video-generators-filmmakers-compared","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b709","text":"For a film-specific comparison of shot control, continuity and editing, read ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b711","text":"AI video generators for filmmakers, compared","marks":["b710"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b712","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}]
35:["$","$L33","post-static-ad-from-style-reference",{"post":{"_key":"post-static-ad-from-style-reference","slug":"static-ad-from-style-reference","category":"guides","title":"How to build a static ad from a style reference on Melius","isoDate":"2026-09-11","date":"September 11, 2026","readTime":"6 Min Read","excerpt":"Point an agent at a moodboard and ask for statics in that style. The brief that does it, what the agent builds in the background, and where you steer.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/static-ad-from-style-reference/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Alex Chen, Member of Technical Staff"}],"faq":[{"question":"Do I have to use the canvas to make static ads on Melius?","answer":"No. You can brief the agent and steer the results, and plenty of people work that way. The canvas is where the agent's work becomes visible and editable, so you'll open it to fix the outputs that missed, but you don't wire the workflow yourself unless you want to."},{"question":"What should I put in the brief?","answer":"The goal, your references, and the constraints that matter: how many variations, which ratios you ship, and the brand anchor to check against. Our example for this workflow is a single sentence asking it to use the Image Style Analysis template with your reference images and return a style description for new variants. Brief the whole job at once rather than one step at a time."},{"question":"Will the agent generate before checking with me?","answer":"That depends on the mode. In ask-permission mode it raises clarifying questions before each major step, which suits high-stakes work where you want to see every decision. In auto-run it decides and builds while you're elsewhere, so a brief sent between meetings has a canvas of results waiting when you get back."},{"question":"How many reference images should I give it?","answer":"Two to four is usually enough, and the recipe works to a range of two to ten. That ceiling is editorial, not technical: individual models accept many more. More references do not produce a more accurate style description, because the analysis describes what your references have in common, so a sixth image sharing less with the others widens the description instead of sharpening it."},{"question":"Can I use a competitor's ad as a style reference?","answer":"Yes, and it's one of the most common inputs for this workflow, alongside your own past campaigns and fashion editorials. The analysis returns a description of photographic qualities such as light, palette and composition rather than a copy of the image, and you're generating your own subject against that description."},{"question":"Can I reuse a style that worked?","answer":"Yes. The style description is a text node, so it copies and pastes between canvases and you can point a later brief at it. Once one reliably produces on-brand output it becomes a small reusable asset you start every campaign canvas from."},{"question":"How much does a batch of static ads cost to run?","answer":"Generating on Melius runs on credits, drawn from the same pool whichever model a step uses, so comparing two models on the same shot costs no more to set up than running one. Current plans and credit allowances are on the pricing page."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"key-takeaways","title":"Key takeaways"},{"_key":"static-ads-that-match-a-look-you-already-have","title":"Match a look"},{"_key":"what-you-actually-type","title":"What you type"},{"_key":"what-the-agent-does-in-the-background","title":"In the background"},{"_key":"where-you-step-in","title":"Where you step in"},{"_key":"where-this-workflow-goes-wrong","title":"Where it goes wrong"},{"_key":"why-the-canvas-is-still-there","title":"Why the canvas"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"FAQ"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b5089","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5088","text":"Key takeaways","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"key-takeaways"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5092","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5090","text":"You brief an agent; you don't wire the workflow. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5091","text":"One instruction naming your references and the output you want is enough. The agent picks the models, writes the prompts, creates the nodes and connects them up.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5095","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5093","text":"The steps still happen, and you can watch them happen. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5094","text":"Reference grouping, style analysis, model choice, variation count: the agent does each one as a visible node rather than behind a loading spinner.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5098","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5096","text":"Expect to finish the last mile yourself. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5097","text":"We put the agent's first pass at 85% to 95% of the way there. The rest is prompt tweaks on individual nodes, and that's where your judgement goes.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5101","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5099","text":"Brief the whole job, not the next step. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5100","text":"Asking for the references, the variations, every ratio and a brand check in one instruction costs the same as asking for one of them.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5104","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5102","text":"Ambiguity gets a question, not a guess. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5103","text":"In ask-permission mode the agent checks aspect ratio, audience and tone before it spends a generation. In auto-run it decides and builds while you're elsewhere.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5106","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5105","text":"Static ads that match a look you already have","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"static-ads-that-match-a-look-you-already-have"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5108","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5107","text":"To build a static ad from a style reference on Melius, you brief the Mel agent: point it at your reference images and ask for new statics in that style. It assembles the canvas, runs the style analysis, chooses the models, generates the variations, and leaves every step visible so you can correct the ones that missed. From brief to assets you can download runs about 10 to 15 minutes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5110","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5109","text":"Most of the work in matching a look goes into describing it. You know the campaign you want to sit next to, and you can see exactly why it works, but turning that into instructions a model will follow is the step that eats an afternoon. That's the step you're handing over.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5112","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5111","text":"What you actually type","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-you-actually-type"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5114","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5113","text":"Right-click anywhere on the canvas and choose Ask Mel, or press the forward slash key. Anything you have selected goes in as a reference automatically. Then describe the job. You don't need to name the model, set the resolution, or say which output connects to which input. Mel will do these for you.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5119","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5116","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5115","text":"Our standing advice is to ask for more than you think will work. A brief naming the references, the number of variations, every ratio you ship and a brand check against your brand anchor costs no more to write than one asking for a single image, and if the agent can't cover the whole job it tells you. Brief it the way you'd brief a designer, with a concrete goal and real constraints, not the way you'd chat. This is the same ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5117","text":"brief-to-execution workflow","marks":["b5116"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5118","text":" applied to a single look.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5121","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5120","text":"What the agent does in the background","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-the-agent-does-in-the-background"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5123","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5122","text":"None of this needs doing by hand, and all of it stays inspectable while it happens. A cyan marker on the canvas shows where the agent is currently building.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5126","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5124","text":"Reads your brand anchor. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5125","text":"If you keep one, the node holding your voice, palette and type gets pulled in as context before anything generates.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5129","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5127","text":"Groups the references. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5128","text":"Your reference images become a single unified group, so the analysis reaches all of them on one edge instead of one per image.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5132","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5130","text":"Runs the style analysis. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5131","text":"The Image Style Analysis template comes preconfigured but has inputs that need wiring, which is exactly the case to hand to the agent. It returns a written description: palette, direction and quality of the light, mood, composition, depth of field, shot type.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5138","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5135","href":"/blog/nano-banana-image-models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5133","text":"Picks the model per step. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5134","text":"Melius recommends ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5136","text":"Nano Banana Pro","marks":["b5135"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5137","text":" for hewing to a photographic look, and GPT Image 2 where the ad carries visible copy, its High tier for production output. You can override that on any node.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5141","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5139","text":"Writes the prompt. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5140","text":"Because the style description carries the look, the generation prompt only has to name the subject and where it sits. Short prompts win here, and the agent knows it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5144","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5142","text":"Builds the image nodes and connects them. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5143","text":"Style description into the image node, resolution set, ratio set per placement. The node hides any ratio the chosen model can't produce.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5147","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5145","text":"Runs the variations in parallel. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5146","text":"Image models are probabilistic, so several takes at once beats one take and a retry. Ask for every ratio in the same brief and it queues those together too.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5149","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5148","text":"Where you step in","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-you-step-in"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5151","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5150","text":"The first pass gets you most of the way, not all of it. We put that at 85% to 95%, and the last stretch is the part worth your attention, because it's taste rather than assembly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5154","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5152","text":"Work at the node, not in the chat. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5153","text":"Open the one image that nearly landed, edit its prompt with the specific correction, and re-run that node alone. Product too small in frame becomes a line saying the product fills 40% of the frame width. Colour drifting green becomes a warmer grade with terracotta in the highlights. Illegible type on a label means switching that node to GPT Image 2 High.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5156","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5155","text":"Go back to the agent for the genuinely bulk things: swapping a model across multiple nodes, regenerating everything with the brand anchor attached, resizing ten nodes into three ratios each.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5158","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5157","text":"One habit worth forming. The agent doesn't automatically know about an edit you made by hand, so if you later ask it to repeat that treatment across the canvas it may revert to its original approach. Either make the change on a shared context node like the brand anchor, where it propagates on the next run, or tell the agent what you changed and ask it to apply that too.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5160","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5159","text":"Where this workflow goes wrong","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"where-this-workflow-goes-wrong"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5163","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5161","text":"The brief was too small. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5162","text":"Describing one step, running it, then describing the next is the safe instinct and it costs you the afternoon. A re-brief is cheap; orchestrating by hand is not.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5166","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5164","text":"The references disagree with each other. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5165","text":"Five fashion editorials and one storefront screenshot do not share a look, and the description will average them into something you didn't ask for. The agent can only describe what your set has in common.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5169","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5167","text":"The agent got treated like a chatbot. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5168","text":"It isn't a chat window, it builds canvases. Conversational back-and-forth gets far less out of it than one concrete brief carrying references and constraints.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5172","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5170","text":"One node got edited fifteen times. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5171","text":"Past about the fifth tweak the problem usually isn't the prompt. Step back and re-brief, because the agent has the whole canvas as context and will often unstick it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5175","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5173","text":"The output was judged on the canvas preview. ","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5174","text":"Previews are downscaled at every resolution to keep the canvas quick. Open a variation full screen, or download it, before you rule it out.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5177","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5176","text":"Why the canvas is still there","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"why-the-canvas-is-still-there"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5179","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5178","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work, and underneath the agent is a node-based canvas where every model call is a node and edges pass one node's output into the next. The canvas isn't something you have to learn before you can work. It's there so the agent's decisions are legible: which model ran, what prompt it wrote, which reference fed which step.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5181","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5180","text":"That's what separates this from describing what you want in a chat and hoping. Nothing here is a black box. When an output is wrong you find the node where it went wrong, change that one thing, and re-run everything downstream of it. Earlier node canvases were built before agents existed and assumed a human would wire up every node; this one exists so you can see and steer the work instead of performing it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5186","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5183","href":"/blog/one-subscription-every-model","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5182","text":"The models sit behind ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5184","text":"one subscription","marks":["b5183"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5185","text":". Melius spans a library of leading models for image, video and audio, and the agent routes each step to the right one unless you choose per node.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5188","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5187","text":"You own the content you create on Melius and can use, publish, and distribute it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms. Melius doesn't claim ownership of your work and doesn't use it to train AI models.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5193","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5190","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5189","text":"Have a look you want to hit? ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5191","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b5190"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5192","text":", drop your references on a canvas, and tell the agent what you want.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5198","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5195","href":"/blog/text-to-speech-voiceover","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5194","text":"For the next step, see ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5196","text":"turning a script into a natural voiceover","marks":["b5195"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5197","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5200","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5199","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b5201","items":"$35:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b5206","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b5203","href":"/blog/product-hero-shot","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b5202","text":"For product photography, follow our ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5204","text":"product hero shot workflow","marks":["b5203"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b5205","text":" to keep specifications, branding, and style references separate.","marks":[]}]}]}}]
